+\section{Bounded Fusion and Residency Exploration}
+\label{sec:s-fusion-residency}
+A subsequent 12-cell, 384-business-request development experiment evaluates six arms on two models and four known task sources. It retains exact Raw/candidate admission, the original margin/EOS floors and PSTP, while separately probing fused execution evidence and revocable certified-prefix priority in the native eviction queue. Priority is capped at 75\% of pool capacity with a 120-s lifetime; it neither changes reference counts nor promises permanent residency.
