+For matched compiled arms, full hits rise from 9/18 to 18/18 under priority; compiled output IDs/EOS remain unchanged. Across all four certificate arms, 72 compiled requests show no ID/EOS changes. Actual reclamation hooks explain the nine strict-arm misses. Fused/residency execution improves Qwen's full workflow but leaves Mistral slower than raw, while Mistral's raw-priority arm improves markedly. Thus the data do not establish a generally beneficial default or a uniquely certified-residency performance effect. The experiment remains a mechanism appendix, with all L0 output variations and failed controls retained.
